WEBVTT

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:08.740
You!

00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:48.160
- Are you serious? - No, just badly shaken up, a little scratch.

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:50.110
- You'll be all right. - Sure.

00:01:50.190 --> 00:01:52.190
Lucky that big piece there didn't suck you.

00:01:52.270 --> 00:01:54.650
- All right, it's all over. Break it up. - How about standing up?

00:01:54.730 --> 00:01:57.120
- Come on, get going. - Yeah.

00:01:57.200 --> 00:02:00.000
- I'm all right, thanks. - Would you like to come with us for a checkup?

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:02.280
I'd better get home to my wife. She worries if I'm late.

00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:03.040
Name and address.

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:08.520
My name is Frank Thompson, 169 North Rutherford.

00:02:08.590 --> 00:02:10.500
Stick around while I pick up a few names of witnesses.

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:14.280
Remember now, if you don't feel so hot, drop in at the hospital and have yourself looked at.

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:15.360
I will, thanks.

00:02:18.610 --> 00:02:27.000
Mister, don't forget your hat.

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:28.460
Oh, thanks.

00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:35.410
- This isn't mine. - Sure it is. I seen it on you when you fell down.

00:02:35.510 --> 00:02:38.030
- What? - Don't you know your own hat, mister?

00:02:38.070 --> 00:02:39.380
Okay now.

00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:41.720
Wait a minute. There's something wrong here, officer.

00:02:42.020 --> 00:02:44.600
This hat and this cigarette case don't belong to me.

00:02:44.920 --> 00:02:47.280
He had that on when he fell down. I seen it.

00:02:47.380 --> 00:02:49.580
- And he took that out of his pocket. - Beat it.

00:02:49.590 --> 00:02:54.070
Say, what part of town is it?

00:02:54.190 --> 00:02:55.670
22nd and Tillery.

00:02:56.050 --> 00:02:58.900
- What am I doing here? - Don't you know?

00:03:00.220 --> 00:03:02.720
I've never been here before in my life.

00:03:02.790 --> 00:03:05.660
There's no reason why I should be here.

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:09.570
I can't even remember how I got here.

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:13.070
You sure you don't want to go someplace and lay down for a little while?

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:15.930
No. I'm gonna get away from here.

00:03:15.940 --> 00:03:19.890
How can I get home? How can I get to North Rutherford Street?

00:03:19.990 --> 00:03:21.490
Well, that's way uptown.

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:23.280
Biel is three blocks over.

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:25.340
East Side Subway is down the street there.

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:27.240
Or you can get the Green Line bus.

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:28.600
Thanks.

00:04:05.340 --> 00:04:12.580
Virginia, Virginia, Virginia!

00:04:16.420 --> 00:04:20.700
Thompson, what are you doing around here?

00:04:20.700 --> 00:04:22.780
Thinking of taking your old flat back?

00:04:22.780 --> 00:04:26.380
It's vacant again. The last tennis moved out only a week ago.

00:04:26.380 --> 00:04:29.410
What are you talking about? What's happened?

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:32.790
- I'm sure I couldn't say what's happened.

00:04:32.790 --> 00:04:34.390
Your wife didn't take me into her confidence

00:04:34.390 --> 00:04:36.100
when she moved away.

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:37.980
- Moved?

00:04:37.980 --> 00:04:39.670
What, I was only this morning

00:04:39.670 --> 00:04:42.530
I said goodbye to her at that very door.

00:04:42.530 --> 00:04:45.200
- I'm sure you're feeling quite well, Mr. Thompson.

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:46.530
- Where's she gone?

00:04:46.530 --> 00:04:47.530
Tell me where I can find her.

00:04:47.530 --> 00:04:48.840
- Please. - Tell me.

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:50.870
- She's living around in Anderson Street.

00:04:50.870 --> 00:04:52.530
Second building from the corner.

00:04:52.530 --> 00:04:54.710
Apartment 4A.

00:05:12.030 --> 00:05:21.330
- Virginia, what is this? What's it all about? - What happened?

00:05:23.560 --> 00:05:30.000
- Apartment. - Your name over the doorbell.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:39.010
- What did you do it for? Why did you move? - What possible reason could you have had to do such a thing without telling me?

00:05:39.010 --> 00:05:45.220
- Frank! Frank! - Virginia, stop it.

00:05:45.220 --> 00:05:49.810
- Frank, I... - I went home. You weren't there. I...

00:05:49.810 --> 00:05:58.120
She told me, Mrs. Webb... Tell me, tell me, there must be some explanation. It doesn't make sense. It's like a bad dream.

00:05:58.120 --> 00:06:00.000
Oh, you've come back, Frank. I knew it.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:05.090
- Why shouldn't I come back? - Come back? From where?

00:06:06.020 --> 00:06:07.620
Why do you say that?

00:06:09.160 --> 00:06:11.140
When I left for the office this morning,

00:06:11.700 --> 00:06:14.660
did I say or do anything that made you think I wasn't coming back?

00:06:14.750 --> 00:06:16.930
- This morning? - Yes.

00:06:17.610 --> 00:06:20.580
You kiss me goodbye, you call out after me.

00:06:21.160 --> 00:06:23.200
Sure you got your muffler? It's cold out.

00:06:23.390 --> 00:06:25.750
Frank, what are you saying this morning?

00:06:26.210 --> 00:06:27.940
I moved here over a year ago.

00:06:32.270 --> 00:06:34.200
The weather alone ought to tell you that.

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:36.370
It's warm out.

00:06:37.740 --> 00:06:40.920
You're not wearing your muffler, or even your coat now.

00:06:40.950 --> 00:06:46.070
You left me in the winter, and now it's spring.

00:06:51.950 --> 00:06:56.450
We've both read of cases like this.

00:06:56.470 --> 00:06:57.860
Amnesia.

00:06:57.880 --> 00:07:00.000
And you waited at the office that last morning.

00:07:00.190 --> 00:07:06.850
something must have happened to you some accident some blow just like what happened tonight you just

00:07:06.850 --> 00:07:13.820
didn't know who you were anymore forgot where you were going forgot to come home to me what

00:07:13.820 --> 00:07:20.850
must you have thought what you must have gone through darling you're back and that's all that

00:07:20.850 --> 00:07:30.000
counts but you how did you manage to get along i got a job several modeling typing in an avatar

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:35.610
agent said I did very well because I haven't been working lately but there's

00:07:35.610 --> 00:07:39.150
enough in the bank to keep us going till you get started again did they ever call

00:07:39.150 --> 00:07:44.010
up from the office naturally I told them you'd had a nervous breakdown I was too

00:07:44.010 --> 00:07:53.460
proud to let anybody know I didn't know where you were that you left me I wonder

00:07:53.460 --> 00:07:58.740
if there's a chance they take me back I don't see why not you were the head of

00:07:58.740 --> 00:07:59.760
your department

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:01.680
Mr. Clark was always terribly fond of you.

00:08:02.110 --> 00:08:02.920
I don't know.

00:08:03.770 --> 00:08:05.180
I don't know which way to turn.

00:08:06.260 --> 00:08:08.440
What to do or what to think.

00:08:10.040 --> 00:08:12.980
I can't remember.

00:08:15.460 --> 00:08:17.320
Don't worry about it tonight.

00:08:18.360 --> 00:08:19.260
Just rest.

00:08:20.960 --> 00:08:22.560
Hold on to the things you're sure of.

00:08:23.690 --> 00:08:24.370
You're home.

00:08:25.100 --> 00:08:25.880
You're safe.

00:08:26.350 --> 00:08:27.320
And I'm with you.

00:08:28.170 --> 00:08:28.610
Hmm.

00:09:30.320 --> 00:09:33.740
I must say, Frank Thompson, you don't look much like you've had a nervous breakdown.

00:09:33.820 --> 00:09:35.910
I'm all right now. Wouldn't be here.

00:09:36.140 --> 00:09:39.600
Yes, sir. Mr. Clark says for you to go right in.

00:09:40.990 --> 00:09:44.020
Well, well, the return of the prodigal.

00:09:44.140 --> 00:09:45.780
- Come right in, Frank. - Thank you.

00:09:45.780 --> 00:09:54.590
You better familiarize yourself with all these new accounts first, Frank.

00:09:54.670 --> 00:09:57.710
- Then we can pick it up from there and you'll be all set. - All right, thanks, Mr. Clark.

00:09:57.790 --> 00:09:59.920
If there's anything else you want to know, just give me a buzz.

00:11:02.910 --> 00:11:07.040
extra paper, extra paper, read all about it.

00:11:33.200 --> 00:11:49.970
- Don't stop! - Sorry, mister. Red light.

00:12:06.040 --> 00:12:20.920
- You didn't have any trouble getting organized at the office today, did you? - Frank, I said you didn't have any trouble remembering today.

00:12:20.920 --> 00:12:26.340
I mean, people and things, the way they were before you went away. Did you?

00:12:26.340 --> 00:12:30.000
That's good. I'm sure.

00:12:30.030 --> 00:12:34.650
- I'm sure you'll be able to recall what happened in that other time. - I hope you're right.

00:12:34.650 --> 00:12:39.490
So lovely out. How would you like to take a little stroll somewhere?

00:12:39.490 --> 00:12:46.070
- Or maybe go to a picture, huh? - No. No, I don't want to go anywhere tonight.

00:12:46.070 --> 00:12:49.390
All right.

00:13:15.900 --> 00:13:16.550
Frank.

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:30.800
Just a moment, please.

00:13:32.090 --> 00:13:32.730
It's your office.

00:13:41.190 --> 00:13:41.430
Hello.

00:13:42.850 --> 00:13:43.710
Oh, yes, Miss Peabody.

00:13:44.400 --> 00:13:46.550
I was working a little late tonight, Mr. Thompson,

00:13:46.650 --> 00:13:48.030
and a call came through for you.

00:13:48.350 --> 00:13:49.790
Someone wanted your telephone number.

00:13:50.230 --> 00:13:50.770
Who was it?

00:13:53.560 --> 00:13:54.360
No name at all?

00:13:55.600 --> 00:13:58.070
No, he just said he was a very old friend of yours.

00:13:58.350 --> 00:14:00.000
He saw you coming out of the building tonight,

00:14:00.090 --> 00:14:01.950
so he came back and made inquiries and...

00:14:01.950 --> 00:14:03.950
You didn't give him my number, did you?

00:14:03.950 --> 00:14:06.000
Well, yes, I did give him the number.

00:14:06.000 --> 00:14:08.000
I hope you don't mind.

00:14:08.000 --> 00:14:10.260
No, not at all. Don't give it another thought.

00:14:10.260 --> 00:14:25.420
Frank, there is something you're keeping from me.

00:14:25.420 --> 00:14:30.000
No, darling. It's only that I can't remember that.

00:16:30.030 --> 00:16:40.860
I'll struggle around the back and watch the fire escapes.

00:16:40.960 --> 00:16:42.960
Virginia, wake up.

00:16:43.060 --> 00:16:45.970
Now, don't be frightened. We've got to get out of here now.

00:16:46.070 --> 00:16:47.530
No light. They might see us.

00:16:47.630 --> 00:16:50.330
There's no time to talk. There's not even time for you to get dressed.

00:16:50.430 --> 00:16:51.930
Just get into your shoes and hurry.

00:16:52.030 --> 00:16:53.930
I'll get your coat. Where's your handbag?

00:16:54.030 --> 00:16:55.220
In the top drawer.

00:17:06.140 --> 00:17:13.860
- Frank what is that? - No time now, fire escape.

00:17:45.520 --> 00:17:47.080
It's locked.

00:17:47.080 --> 00:17:58.120
Next building, come on.

00:17:58.120 --> 00:18:00.000
Frank, you've got to tell me, what's this all about?

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:01.540
We're not out of it yet.

00:18:35.210 --> 00:18:38.880
- Sorry, darling, but I'm all in.

00:18:38.880 --> 00:18:47.290
- There's what we want.

00:18:47.290 --> 00:18:50.190
- Get in.

00:18:50.190 --> 00:18:51.270
I want you to go to your mother's

00:18:51.270 --> 00:18:53.000
and stay there until you hear from me.

00:18:53.000 --> 00:18:53.840
- No.

00:18:53.840 --> 00:18:55.510
- At least whatever happens, I'll know you're safe.

00:18:55.510 --> 00:18:58.050
And don't try to get in touch with me in any way.

00:18:58.050 --> 00:19:00.000
I don't know who they are or why they're after me.

00:19:00.510 --> 00:19:04.310
- I only know that I've got to keep you out of this. - Please, Frank, I'm not afraid.

00:19:04.390 --> 00:19:06.590
- Let me see it through with you. - No.

00:19:06.670 --> 00:19:10.750
When a man falls in quicksand, he doesn't reach up and pull those he loves down with him.

00:19:10.830 --> 00:19:17.540
Goodbye for now. I've got to find out what this is before I dare come into your life again.

00:19:17.620 --> 00:19:19.540
If you love me, you'll do what I ask you.

00:19:19.620 --> 00:19:22.340
I won't have a moment's rest until I see you again.

00:19:22.420 --> 00:19:26.890
- Until I hear you say that everything is all right. - Please, God, that won't be long.

00:19:26.970 --> 00:19:30.000
Where to, folks? Round the park for two bucks.

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:32.720
- I'll tell you where she wants to go. - Okay.

00:19:32.800 --> 00:19:34.840
- Goodbye for a little. - Goodbye, Donald.

00:21:06.010 --> 00:21:27.680
"Somewhere down here's the answer. Some place there's somebody that's got to recognize me. Remember me. Say hello. Nobody I ever saw in my life. Nobody that ever saw me from the looks on their faces."

00:21:31.760 --> 00:21:32.640
That's what I can use.

00:21:45.390 --> 00:21:59.280
Hey, could you give me any more?

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:07.260
this again, huh? Why, is this the same place I brought it before? I mean, you know, all these

00:22:07.260 --> 00:22:12.650
pawn shops look alike to me. Three times you've been in here with this now. To me, this is the

00:22:12.650 --> 00:22:18.160
best-known cigarette case in the neighborhood. Said you keep the ticket stubs or whatever they're

00:22:18.160 --> 00:22:23.090
called after the article's been once redeemed? Sure. What address are you going to give me this time?

00:22:23.530 --> 00:22:30.000
What address did I give you last time? A phony, a vacant lot. Say, who did you think you was foolish?

00:22:30.640 --> 00:22:33.340
- I looked it up. - Nobody.

00:22:33.340 --> 00:22:36.930
- How much? - Four dollars.

00:22:36.930 --> 00:22:38.930
Losing money.

00:23:27.740 --> 00:23:28.200
I'll go next.

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:31.000
I haven't been in here lately.

00:23:31.530 --> 00:23:32.230
You've been here before?

00:23:33.180 --> 00:23:34.620
Sure. Don't you recognize me?

00:23:35.240 --> 00:23:36.240
We get a lot of people here.

00:23:36.600 --> 00:23:38.200
Yes, sir. Come right in. Sit down. No waiting.

00:23:38.710 --> 00:23:48.880
Come in, mister. No waiting.

00:23:49.570 --> 00:23:51.010
What do you mean, no waiting?

00:23:55.120 --> 00:23:59.190
All day long walking up and down this cockeyed street.

00:24:02.940 --> 00:24:04.140
Not a peep out of anybody.

00:24:06.850 --> 00:24:10.770
Listen, I've got to find something that'll help me remember.

00:24:11.950 --> 00:24:15.680
Maybe if I had a drink, something called beer.

00:24:45.800 --> 00:24:47.670
that be? You ought to know by now.

00:24:49.220 --> 00:24:52.200
What do you want, mister? Beer.

00:24:53.490 --> 00:24:54.900
Say something, first of all.

00:26:04.060 --> 00:26:07.770
Crazy fool, what are you doing on the open street like this?

00:26:08.540 --> 00:26:11.120
Well, I was watching the fire.

00:26:11.420 --> 00:26:12.620
Have you lost your mind?

00:26:13.020 --> 00:26:14.920
Come on inside before somebody sees you.

00:26:15.200 --> 00:26:16.760
What are you trying to do, throw yourself away?

00:26:17.080 --> 00:26:18.620
Don't you know crowds are the worst place for you?

00:26:18.860 --> 00:26:20.460
Get into the apartment, quick. Hurry.

00:26:20.860 --> 00:26:22.820
I'll look around, see if anyone's tailing you.

00:26:31.280 --> 00:26:33.340
- Danny, where are you going? - Well, I...

00:26:33.420 --> 00:26:35.220
What's the matter with you? Go on up.

00:27:12.320 --> 00:27:15.340
Danny, you'd better keep away from that window.

00:27:15.760 --> 00:27:17.960
What are you doing in this part of town, anyway?

00:27:18.060 --> 00:27:20.260
Don't you realize they've been watching you too?

00:27:20.360 --> 00:27:22.540
Well, I had to come back to find out things.

00:27:22.620 --> 00:27:24.380
Well, haven't you been reading the papers?

00:27:24.600 --> 00:27:28.710
Yes, sure, but you must know more than I do.

00:27:29.100 --> 00:27:30.000
All I know is...

00:27:30.000 --> 00:27:32.420
that Joe Marucci has sworn to get you.

00:27:32.960 --> 00:27:33.750
Joe Marucci?

00:27:33.890 --> 00:27:34.490
Oh, Dan.

00:27:34.990 --> 00:27:37.790
Dan, darling, you don't know what it's been like these last few days.

00:27:40.400 --> 00:27:41.360
Aren't you gonna kiss me?

00:27:47.090 --> 00:27:48.370
Why are you so worried about me?

00:27:48.870 --> 00:27:50.140
Why am I so...

00:27:50.140 --> 00:27:50.860
Oh, you.

00:27:51.510 --> 00:27:53.220
Why do I love you like this?

00:27:53.280 --> 00:27:54.840
You're no good and you never will be.

00:27:56.310 --> 00:27:58.130
Dan, what are we gonna do?

00:27:58.670 --> 00:27:59.420
You gotta help me.

00:27:59.560 --> 00:28:00.000
I know.

00:28:00.540 --> 00:28:03.640
I know, I've been racking my brain trying to think how.

00:28:05.340 --> 00:28:10.900
Give me a cigarette, and let's just be happy together for a few minutes anyway.

00:28:12.380 --> 00:28:15.530
We may never have another chance.

00:28:20.540 --> 00:28:23.090
Wait, I want to make a wish.

00:28:23.900 --> 00:28:29.250
There, you ought to know what it was, that they'll never get you.

00:28:30.000 --> 00:28:37.040
let me keep you like this to myself forever forever is a long time how long's it been now

00:28:37.040 --> 00:28:46.170
seem to have lost track of time a little a week just one little week all our plans all our dreams

00:28:46.170 --> 00:28:56.360
gone simply because because let's not talk about it i want to talk about it i want you to go over

00:28:56.360 --> 00:29:00.000
everything with me so it'll all be clear so i'll know where i stand what

00:29:00.000 --> 00:29:03.520
- What to do next? - Danny, what a strange thing for you to say.

00:29:03.660 --> 00:29:07.050
- What is there to go over? - There's a lot of things to go over.

00:29:07.080 --> 00:29:11.420
- I think what we both need is a drink. - Amen to that.

00:29:11.540 --> 00:29:14.050
Help me up. Have you had your dinner?

00:29:14.230 --> 00:29:16.840
Well, I haven't. Wait till I see what's in the kitchen.

00:29:38.090 --> 00:29:41.250
There isn't a thing to eat in here or to drink, either.

00:29:41.330 --> 00:29:44.950
- You know how it is, using this place only once a week on my day off. - Sure.

00:29:45.030 --> 00:29:47.700
I think I'll run down the corner and get something and bring it up here.

00:29:47.790 --> 00:29:50.480
- What would you like to drink? - I don't care. Beer?

00:29:50.560 --> 00:29:52.490
All right, I'll see if they have some on ice.

00:29:52.740 --> 00:29:56.590
- I'd better lock this after me. - Afraid I'll get out, Ruth?

00:29:57.090 --> 00:30:00.000
Oh, no, Mr. Nearing. Afraid somebody might get in.

00:31:40.910 --> 00:31:43.740
- I heard her come in, but I guess she went out. - Thank you.

00:31:55.920 --> 00:31:59.700
Good evening.

00:32:02.170 --> 00:32:05.030
- What do you want? - You think you're a pretty smart girl, don't you?

00:32:05.080 --> 00:32:08.500
- Meaning what? - Tipping your boyfriend off last night that we're gonna move in on him.

00:32:08.550 --> 00:32:12.930
How would I know that? Besides, if you'll take the trouble to check,

00:32:13.140 --> 00:32:16.080
you'll find that I was in New Jericho last night.

00:32:16.160 --> 00:32:19.810
Well, if you were, then you can't be living uptown under the name of Virginia Morrison.

00:32:19.930 --> 00:32:25.060
- What? - Virginia Morrison. It's a name over the doorbell where he was hiding out.

00:32:25.490 --> 00:32:30.000
- You mean he didn't mention Virginia? - He doesn't know any Virginias.

00:32:31.020 --> 00:32:33.100
Rats like Danny Nearing never cheat.

00:32:33.180 --> 00:32:36.060
They may carve up helpless old men and steal their dough,

00:32:36.140 --> 00:32:38.400
but they never, never know any Virginians

00:32:38.480 --> 00:32:40.380
when they're going around with dames named Ruth.

00:32:40.460 --> 00:32:43.560
Oh, no, I know that one, that old jealousy gag.

00:32:43.640 --> 00:32:45.720
Boyfriend chisels, girl,

00:32:45.800 --> 00:32:49.930
wised up by sympathetic officer of the law, burns and tells all.

00:32:50.010 --> 00:32:52.890
If you've come all the way down here to shake the mothballs out of that one,

00:32:52.970 --> 00:32:54.390
you've wasted your time.

00:32:54.480 --> 00:32:56.370
The commissioner wants to see me find.

00:32:56.450 --> 00:33:00.000
- I hope the record interviews are out. - All this won't take up much of your time.

00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:01.900
Just how far the law allows you to go.

00:33:02.000 --> 00:33:04.100
And this is as far as you're going without a warrant.

00:33:04.200 --> 00:33:06.600
- You're just making things tough for yourself. - Good night.

00:33:06.700 --> 00:33:08.080
Take your foot out of the door.

00:33:08.180 --> 00:33:10.780
I think I'm going to have you picked up as a material witness.

00:33:10.880 --> 00:33:12.710
Fine. Get Virginia, too.

00:33:50.860 --> 00:33:51.990
Here's your beer.

00:33:52.020 --> 00:33:53.970
Oh, I see you found the clippings.

00:33:54.030 --> 00:33:56.020
I've been saving them for you.

00:33:56.300 --> 00:33:59.220
- Anything there you haven't seen before? - Yes.

00:34:00.000 --> 00:34:06.640
Ruth, you don't believe that I killed him, do you?

00:34:06.740 --> 00:34:09.490
Danny, I wasn't there.

00:34:09.590 --> 00:34:15.350
- Where were you? - In the bar mixing drinks for Bill and Alma, as usual.

00:34:15.450 --> 00:34:17.970
Bill and Alma?

00:34:18.070 --> 00:34:21.560
Yes, he was in her sitting room, also, as usual.

00:34:21.660 --> 00:34:25.990
They swore they heard you and Dietrich yelling at each other all the way upstairs.

00:34:26.090 --> 00:34:30.000
They couldn't have. I was in the next room and I didn't hear you.

00:34:30.000 --> 00:34:33.920
Dan, if only you hadn't run away.

00:34:34.000 --> 00:34:37.230
But that was my fault. It was the worst possible advice.

00:34:37.310 --> 00:34:41.180
- But I thought... - That I did it?

00:34:41.260 --> 00:34:45.180
Dan, it doesn't matter. I don't care whether you killed him or not.

00:34:45.260 --> 00:34:48.650
- Then you will help me? - You don't have to ask me that.

00:34:48.730 --> 00:34:52.260
I love you. I'll help you get away if it's the last thing I ever do.

00:34:52.340 --> 00:34:55.150
- You're really me now? - With all my heart.

00:34:55.230 --> 00:34:59.090
Danny...

00:35:00.730 --> 00:35:07.110
- Could you hear what Marucci was saying to me out in the hall? - Yes, some of it.

00:35:07.110 --> 00:35:14.950
- Why do you look at me like that? - Virginia.

00:35:14.950 --> 00:35:20.770
- Who? Virginia, yes. Yes, I heard that. - Well, whose apartment were you hiding in?

00:35:20.770 --> 00:35:24.860
A friend of mine. I mean, a girlfriend of a friend of mine.

00:35:24.860 --> 00:35:26.860
Her name's Virginia. - Oh.

00:35:26.860 --> 00:35:30.000
She wasn't there. She was out of town. He let me use the price.

00:35:30.120 --> 00:35:32.820
That's that name over the doorbell, Virginia Morrison.

00:35:33.030 --> 00:35:36.860
Is that all she is to you, just a name over a doorbell?

00:35:36.940 --> 00:35:44.970
- That's all. - All right, Danny.

00:35:45.040 --> 00:35:48.400
You ought to have a good sock in the jaw.

00:35:48.400 --> 00:35:50.520
Go ahead, sock me.

00:35:50.850 --> 00:35:56.080
Danny, I'd go through anything for you, but never lie to me.

00:35:56.080 --> 00:35:59.250
Ruth.

00:36:00.220 --> 00:36:03.070
- I didn't kill Dietrich. - I couldn't have.

00:36:03.240 --> 00:36:07.080
I'm not a murderer. The me that's inside wouldn't let me kill anyone.

00:36:07.220 --> 00:36:09.820
- But I got to find out. - How?

00:36:09.990 --> 00:36:13.090
- I'm going up... - What?

00:36:13.370 --> 00:36:16.170
- Danny, you're crazy. - Sooner or later, the police are going to catch up with me.

00:36:16.370 --> 00:36:18.690
- I've got to find out what I can before they do. - No.

00:36:18.890 --> 00:36:20.870
- No, I won't let you. - You're going to help me.

00:36:21.010 --> 00:36:23.010
You said a minute ago you'd go through anything for me.

00:36:23.210 --> 00:36:26.180
- All right, prove it. - But Bill and Alma,

00:36:26.520 --> 00:36:28.320
don't you see they're trying to pin this on you?

00:36:28.520 --> 00:36:30.000
- Why? - Well, you know why.

00:36:30.090 --> 00:36:33.890
Because they'll inherit everything if they can keep suspicion away from themselves.

00:36:34.090 --> 00:36:35.350
You mean one of them did it?

00:36:35.530 --> 00:36:37.990
I don't know, but who else could it have been?

00:36:38.190 --> 00:36:39.990
There was only you and me and the cook.

00:36:40.190 --> 00:36:41.990
We'll find out whether they did it or not.

00:36:42.150 --> 00:36:44.800
Somewhere in that house is the right answer.

00:36:44.910 --> 00:36:47.520
And I've got to find it. We've got to find it.

00:36:48.190 --> 00:36:51.160
I've just come from there and tomorrow's my day off.

00:36:51.360 --> 00:36:53.760
- What'll they say? - You'll have to think up something good.

00:36:54.260 --> 00:37:00.000
- What trains are there? - There's one at 9:25, I think, but...

00:37:00.000 --> 00:37:02.950
- Danny! Danny! - That's the one we'll be on.

00:37:03.050 --> 00:37:12.980
I don't think I should answer that question unless my attorney is present.

00:37:13.080 --> 00:37:16.100
- That's your privilege, Mr. Deidre. - Bill, don't talk like a ninny.

00:37:16.200 --> 00:37:20.490
After all, this is just an informal little get-together to help me,

00:37:20.590 --> 00:37:24.790
as District Attorney of Jericho County, tie up the loose ends of my report for the grand jury.

00:37:24.890 --> 00:37:27.590
I have nothing to add to what I've already told you.

00:37:27.690 --> 00:37:30.000
You ain't told us very much, Mr. Deidre.

00:37:32.460 --> 00:37:36.910
example i'm still not quite sure where you all were when the crime occurred i was getting ready

00:37:36.910 --> 00:37:43.120
for bed brushing your teeth and whatnot exactly how long has it been your habit to brush your

00:37:43.120 --> 00:37:51.060
teeth in mrs didrick's private sitting room look here still deposition of ruth dylan made in part

00:37:51.060 --> 00:37:55.420
young mr bill was with mrs didrick in her upstairs sitting room they told me to go down

00:37:55.420 --> 00:38:00.000
to the bar and mix two bourbon highballs as usual they also asked me

00:38:00.000 --> 00:38:02.530
to look and see if Mr. Harry Dietrich was still in the living room.

00:38:02.530 --> 00:38:06.610
- Now, surely, Mr. Dietrich, in the light of what you've just told me... - She's lying.

00:38:06.690 --> 00:38:11.200
That would be perjury, Mr. Dietrich. That there is a sworn statement.

00:38:11.280 --> 00:38:14.240
She'd do anything to protect Neering. She's crazy about him.

00:38:14.910 --> 00:38:16.740
Yes, we have ample proof of that.

00:38:17.300 --> 00:38:20.520
At the moment, though, let us confine ourselves to the situation in your home

00:38:20.600 --> 00:38:22.760
as it existed prior to your brother's murder.

00:38:22.760 --> 00:38:27.270
Situation? He means you and me, Bill.

00:38:27.730 --> 00:38:30.000
- Alma, you don't know what you're saying. - Oh, yes, I do.

00:38:30.000 --> 00:38:33.750
I do. Bill and I have been in love with each other for a long time, Mr. Stillwell.

00:38:33.800 --> 00:38:35.800
Of course, it's all been perfectly proper.

00:38:35.880 --> 00:38:39.830
I was on the point of discussing a divorce arrangement with my husband when he...

00:38:40.780 --> 00:38:41.970
He didn't know then?

00:38:42.060 --> 00:38:46.730
Oh, no. No, we've always been extremely careful not to hurt him, I mean.

00:38:47.030 --> 00:38:50.110
And yet, the day before he was killed, he'd instructed his lawyer

00:38:50.190 --> 00:38:52.560
to draw up a new will, cutting you off of the dollar.

00:38:52.920 --> 00:38:54.820
I wonder why.

00:38:54.920 --> 00:38:57.430
Of course, he was dead before the new will could be executed.

00:38:57.710 --> 00:38:59.640
Poor Harry.

00:39:00.640 --> 00:39:02.840
You're familiar, I suppose, with the amount of the estate?

00:39:02.850 --> 00:39:06.940
- More or less. - More or less, about $250,000.

00:39:07.040 --> 00:39:10.280
- Really? - Money, money, money.

00:39:10.420 --> 00:39:12.000
The root of all evil.

00:39:12.760 --> 00:39:14.940
- Especially if you ain't got none. - What's that?

00:39:15.040 --> 00:39:18.600
Oh, nothing. Not a darn thing. I'm just philosophizing it myself.

00:39:19.130 --> 00:39:22.770
Uh, tell me, Mrs. Diedrich, have you ever discussed this matter

00:39:22.870 --> 00:39:24.480
with your late husband's brother?

00:39:24.500 --> 00:39:27.360
- You don't have to answer that question, Alma. - I don't intend to.

00:39:27.520 --> 00:39:30.000
I think you're rather exceeding your authority at this point.

00:39:30.120 --> 00:39:31.950
Mr. Stillwell. We're not in court,

00:39:32.050 --> 00:39:33.850
please remember. You misinterpret my

00:39:33.850 --> 00:39:35.610
question, Mrs. Dietrich. Do I?

00:39:36.090 --> 00:39:37.810
Perhaps from now on you'd better address your

00:39:37.810 --> 00:39:39.850
questions to our attorney. Definitely. As you

00:39:39.850 --> 00:39:41.650
wish. And thank you so much for coming.

00:39:42.240 --> 00:39:43.840
Hello, Joe. I thought you were staying down

00:39:43.840 --> 00:39:45.860
in the city today. You're just the people I want to

00:39:45.860 --> 00:39:47.740
see. It's very late and I'm very tired,

00:39:47.860 --> 00:39:49.780
Mr. Marucci. There's a couple of questions I want to ask you

00:39:49.780 --> 00:39:51.800
about your maid, Ruth Dillon. But Mrs. Dietrich

00:39:51.800 --> 00:39:53.780
and her brother-in-law have just declined to answer any further

00:39:53.780 --> 00:39:55.380
questions, except through their lawyer.

00:39:55.730 --> 00:39:57.770
This is a night off, isn't it? Supposed to be in

00:39:57.770 --> 00:40:00.000
town? I just saw her down at the

00:40:00.000 --> 00:40:03.160
- She's at the station, getting off to 9:25. - Oh.

00:40:03.160 --> 00:40:05.700
- Any idea why she should be coming back? - Not in the least.

00:40:05.700 --> 00:40:10.780
- Good night, Mr. Marucci. - I still say that dame ought to be picked up and held as a material witness.

00:40:10.780 --> 00:40:15.470
- No! - Mrs. Dietrich maintains that if we allow the girl to move about freely,

00:40:15.470 --> 00:40:18.410
she might accidentally tip us off as to where Neering is hiding out.

00:40:18.410 --> 00:40:22.820
- There's some logic in that. - You're the boss.

00:40:22.820 --> 00:40:24.860
- Got a gun up at the house? - Yes.

00:40:24.860 --> 00:40:29.800
- Keep it handy. And lock your bedroom door. - You mean there's apt to be trouble?

00:40:30.030 --> 00:40:31.910
I hope so. Quick and plentiful.

00:40:32.030 --> 00:40:34.490
I'm getting sick and tired of the way this case is being run.

00:40:35.020 --> 00:40:35.840
If that'll be all.

00:40:36.610 --> 00:40:38.290
Yes, until I can get in touch with your lawyer.

00:40:38.710 --> 00:40:39.220
Good night.

00:40:39.500 --> 00:40:40.020
Good night.

00:40:42.670 --> 00:40:45.990
When the Dillon dame got off the train,

00:40:46.070 --> 00:40:48.190
she caught a ride to the Diedrich house on a truck.

00:40:48.570 --> 00:40:49.060
So what?

00:40:49.550 --> 00:40:52.370
So I'd like to find out if she finished the ride alone

00:40:52.370 --> 00:40:54.270
or if she picked up somebody further on.

00:41:22.490 --> 00:41:24.530
- It's all right, they're out. - Where do you think they are?

00:41:24.610 --> 00:41:27.890
Well, you know them when they go out, the country club or just park somewhere...

00:41:27.970 --> 00:41:29.960
...having a little talk about life.

00:41:30.480 --> 00:41:32.360
- We've lots of time. - Let me see that light.

00:41:32.370 --> 00:41:35.080
- Now. - I just want to look around.

00:41:35.090 --> 00:41:37.910
Now that we're here, what do you think you're gonna find, for heaven's sakes?

00:41:37.990 --> 00:41:41.440
I don't know. See, now, this would be the living room, of course.

00:41:41.520 --> 00:41:44.470
You ought to know, after all the months you've worked here.

00:41:44.470 --> 00:41:46.880
I get a little confused in the dark.

00:41:46.900 --> 00:41:50.360
That doesn't make any more sense than some of the other things you've been saying.

00:41:50.370 --> 00:41:52.440
- It's the front door? - Yes.

00:41:52.440 --> 00:41:55.190
That's where it's been for the last 50 years.

00:41:55.190 --> 00:41:59.640
- The bar and solarium over there and the alcove where... - Where it happened?

00:42:01.440 --> 00:42:05.170
- You certainly don't want to go back in there, do you? - That's just where I do want to go.

00:42:05.340 --> 00:42:07.710
- You'll go alone. - Why?

00:42:08.350 --> 00:42:10.650
Only two things would take anybody in there.

00:42:10.730 --> 00:42:14.250
A morbid mind or a completely hard-boiled way of looking at life.

00:42:14.370 --> 00:42:16.590
- I don't happen to have either. - I'm hard-boiled.

00:42:16.670 --> 00:42:19.530
Or insane. You wouldn't have come back here if you weren't.

00:42:19.660 --> 00:42:22.010
Tell you what, Ruth, go to the bar and get me a shot of brandy, will you?

00:42:22.090 --> 00:42:23.970
I'm not feeling as hard-boiled as you think.

00:42:24.080 --> 00:42:27.980
Right now, I'm not so sure what I think. No lights, remember.

00:42:28.330 --> 00:42:30.000
Don't go too far. Don't be gone too long.

00:43:56.750 --> 00:43:58.160
- What is it? - What happened?

00:44:01.050 --> 00:44:04.990
- How can I help it? - Do you suppose if there'd been anybody upstairs, they'd have heard?

00:44:05.070 --> 00:44:10.370
- Naturally. - Well, you remember, you said on the night of the murder, you didn't hear anything from the bar,

00:44:10.470 --> 00:44:13.290
but Bill and Alma swore they did and they were all the way upstairs.

00:44:13.390 --> 00:44:16.580
- Proving what? - Well, proving that you're right, that nobody yelled at all.

00:44:17.140 --> 00:44:23.700
Do you mean to say that you scared me out of a year's growth just to... you! You!

00:44:23.760 --> 00:44:28.580
What's the matter with you? If you're gonna fly off the handle this way, you're not gonna be much help.

00:44:28.860 --> 00:44:30.000
What do you expect me to do?

00:44:30.060 --> 00:44:31.420
when you play tricks like that on me.

00:44:32.210 --> 00:44:35.120
Oh, Dan, Dan, don't do a thing like that again.

00:44:35.280 --> 00:44:36.120
All right, I promise.

00:44:36.870 --> 00:44:38.330
You see, I just had to try it.

00:44:38.800 --> 00:44:39.700
Now, how about my drink?

00:44:41.070 --> 00:44:42.850
I ought to mix you a Mickey.

00:44:42.850 --> 00:44:43.570
Mickey.

00:45:22.840 --> 00:45:24.580
There's an old woman in there. She saw me.

00:45:24.650 --> 00:45:26.740
That's only Grandma Dietrich Silly here.

00:45:26.860 --> 00:45:30.000
- Grandma Dietrich? - You're certainly not worried about her.

00:45:30.480 --> 00:45:31.920
Well, she'll tell everybody she saw me.

00:45:33.040 --> 00:45:34.880
Say, what is the matter with you, anyway?

00:45:35.610 --> 00:45:37.570
Ever since I dragged you in off the street this evening,

00:45:37.650 --> 00:45:39.690
you've been making some of the strangest cracks.

00:45:40.090 --> 00:45:42.730
Well, you know what a terrible strain I've been under.

00:45:42.770 --> 00:45:46.290
I know, but getting all upset about a harmless old woman who...

00:45:46.290 --> 00:45:48.330
What is it? Tell me. What's happened to you?

00:45:48.890 --> 00:45:50.610
I get frightened when you say such things.

00:45:50.750 --> 00:45:52.630
It sounds like you're cracking up.

00:45:53.640 --> 00:45:56.730
All right. All right, I'll tell you.

00:45:58.040 --> 00:45:59.760
I hadn't wanted to tell you because...

00:46:00.860 --> 00:46:05.030
It's not easy to believe, but on the street the other day...

00:46:05.540 --> 00:46:08.310
- I was hit on the head. - Oh, Danny.

00:46:08.390 --> 00:46:11.840
I did, I swear. It was something from a building.

00:46:11.980 --> 00:46:14.290
And you haven't been able to remember anything since.

00:46:14.370 --> 00:46:16.290
To a certain extent, that's exactly right.

00:46:16.370 --> 00:46:19.250
- Especially about the Dietrichs. - You gotta believe me, Ruth.

00:46:19.330 --> 00:46:21.250
- Oh, I do. I do. - And you gotta try to help me remember...

00:46:21.330 --> 00:46:25.750
- ...and certain questions will sound nonsensical. - Sure, any little thing you want.

00:46:25.850 --> 00:46:29.560
- Ruth. - Too bad you weren't hit on the head before Harry Dietrich was killed.

00:46:31.950 --> 00:46:34.100
Oh, Dan, I'm sorry. I shouldn't have said that.

00:46:34.210 --> 00:46:36.170
Forgive me. Kiss me and forgive me.

00:46:36.180 --> 00:46:53.240
I've got to look around some more. Don't be frightened.

00:47:18.680 --> 00:47:23.370
You know who I am? Danny Nearing.

00:47:25.220 --> 00:47:26.690
I want to talk to you.

00:47:28.780 --> 00:47:30.000
Harry Dietrich was

00:47:30.250 --> 00:47:31.380
Your son, wasn't he?

00:47:32.120 --> 00:47:34.100
I didn't kill him. I couldn't have.

00:47:34.670 --> 00:47:35.910
I want you to know that.

00:47:36.560 --> 00:47:40.090
I've come back to this house with the police practically breathing down my neck

00:47:40.090 --> 00:47:41.360
to find who did.

00:47:42.250 --> 00:47:44.270
I don't know where to start. I don't know what to do.

00:47:44.840 --> 00:47:47.160
I need someone to help me, and there isn't anyone.

00:48:27.930 --> 00:48:28.420
Sorry.

00:48:30.030 --> 00:48:33.080
and realize you can't talk.

00:48:33.960 --> 00:48:35.300
You would help me if you could.

00:48:40.850 --> 00:48:42.300
It's like too strong.

00:48:46.660 --> 00:48:47.040
Yeah.

00:48:48.450 --> 00:48:48.690
Better?

00:48:52.770 --> 00:48:55.250
You understand everything I say, don't you?

00:48:58.920 --> 00:48:59.870
You mean you do?

00:49:03.160 --> 00:49:08.550
one blink means yes, two blinks could mean no then, couldn't it?

00:49:08.550 --> 00:49:10.870
Well now we're getting somewhere.

00:49:10.870 --> 00:49:13.660
Mrs. Dietrich, I'm going to ask you a lot of questions.

00:49:13.660 --> 00:49:16.040
You can answer yes or no just like that.

00:49:16.040 --> 00:49:23.120
One blink for yes, two blinks for...

00:49:23.120 --> 00:49:25.220
Danny, what are you up to now?

00:49:25.220 --> 00:49:27.220
What's that lamp lit for? Are you crazy?

00:49:27.220 --> 00:49:29.380
No, wait a minute, that's all right, I've drawn the blinds.

00:49:29.380 --> 00:49:30.000
I've just made it...

00:49:30.000 --> 00:49:32.280
a discovery. I think I found a way to talk to her.

00:49:32.400 --> 00:49:34.280
What? We've worked out a system. One blink for yes,

00:49:34.380 --> 00:49:36.300
two blinks for known. Now watch this. Oh, Danny,

00:49:36.420 --> 00:49:37.940
leave her alone. She's sick.

00:49:38.430 --> 00:49:39.790
Would you like me to turn your pillow?

00:49:40.600 --> 00:49:42.600
It's a shame the way they neglect her since Harry

00:49:42.600 --> 00:49:44.760
died. She really ought to have a nurse.

00:49:45.150 --> 00:49:46.570
I don't know what she'll do now that we're

00:49:46.570 --> 00:49:49.180
leaving. Leaving? Yes.

00:49:49.400 --> 00:49:51.360
No. Once you've satisfied yourself that there's

00:49:51.360 --> 00:49:53.260
nothing in this house that can help you, and if the

00:49:53.260 --> 00:49:54.750
police don't grab you, we're going away.

00:49:54.750 --> 00:49:56.970
I know a place in Colorado that's...

00:49:56.970 --> 00:49:59.290
Fine chance we've got to get to Colorado with every road in the state

00:49:59.290 --> 00:50:00.000
being watched. We've

00:50:00.000 --> 00:50:02.540
can do anything with enough money, and I've got some.

00:50:02.620 --> 00:50:03.620
I've saved it for us.

00:50:03.660 --> 00:50:05.200
Listen, what's that?

00:50:06.960 --> 00:50:10.420
It's a car coming up to the drive.

00:50:10.580 --> 00:50:11.480
It's Alma and Bill.

00:50:11.900 --> 00:50:12.940
Now we're in for it.

00:50:14.040 --> 00:50:15.250
I'll put the car away.

00:50:15.310 --> 00:50:15.950
Have you got your key?

00:50:16.130 --> 00:50:16.410
Yes.

00:50:16.710 --> 00:50:18.640
You might have a drink ready for me when I get in.

00:50:18.740 --> 00:50:19.200
All right.

00:50:19.200 --> 00:50:19.520
All right.

00:50:49.840 --> 00:50:51.520
What's going on in here?

00:50:51.520 --> 00:50:53.320
Oh, good evening, Mrs. Dietrich.

00:50:53.320 --> 00:50:54.910
What are you doing back from town?

00:50:54.910 --> 00:50:57.720
Well, I have something I want to talk to you about.

00:50:57.720 --> 00:51:00.000
It must be tremendously important to have brought you back

00:51:00.000 --> 00:51:03.020
Well, as soon as you finish fussing with Grandma,

00:51:03.020 --> 00:51:05.020
you'll find me in the sunroom.

00:51:05.020 --> 00:51:07.030
Good night, Grandma.

00:51:07.030 --> 00:51:20.710
Yes, Mrs. Dietrich.

00:51:20.710 --> 00:51:22.740
Ruth, how did this happen to be here?

00:51:22.740 --> 00:51:24.730
Oh, I'm sorry, that's mine.

00:51:24.730 --> 00:51:28.390
The reason I came up here tonight was to tell you that I'm leaving.

00:51:28.390 --> 00:51:29.960
- You're leaving? - Yes.

00:51:30.060 --> 00:51:32.220
Well, I hope you don't plan to go too far away,

00:51:32.300 --> 00:51:34.500
because the police might not approve exactly.

00:51:34.850 --> 00:51:37.720
I can go anywhere I please. They have my statement.

00:52:00.000 --> 00:52:02.900
I'll sneak you through the kitchen, into the yard, and join you as soon as I can.

00:52:03.000 --> 00:52:04.700
Better turn out that light. Be careful.

00:52:04.710 --> 00:52:15.510
We'll try it again later tomorrow. First chance I get.

00:52:37.160 --> 00:52:40.560
- Oh, good evening, Mr. Dietrich. - Well, I heard you'd come back from town.

00:52:40.660 --> 00:52:42.700
- Who told you? - Joe Marucci.

00:52:42.900 --> 00:52:45.100
He seems to be quite fascinated by your movements.

00:52:45.390 --> 00:52:47.410
I can't say that I blame him.

00:52:48.350 --> 00:52:51.750
- Mrs. Dietrich's waiting for me at the bar. - Oh, do you mind if I join you?

00:52:52.170 --> 00:52:56.070
- How did this happen? - Oh, I dropped it.

00:52:56.440 --> 00:53:00.000
- Why? - Well, I, um, I was getting a little brandy

00:53:00.000 --> 00:53:03.680
for Grandmother Dietrich when I heard a noise that startled me.

00:53:03.760 --> 00:53:06.400
- What sort of a noise? - Well, it sounded like a cry

00:53:06.480 --> 00:53:08.120
and it came from the alcove.

00:53:08.200 --> 00:53:11.520
Nonsense. So you helped yourself to another drink, two of them.

00:53:11.600 --> 00:53:14.240
One was for your mother-in-law, Mrs. Dietrich.

00:53:14.320 --> 00:53:16.860
I see, of course. You're a clever girl, Ruth.

00:53:16.940 --> 00:53:19.760
- I always suspected as much. - What is all this?

00:53:19.840 --> 00:53:22.320
What was it you were saying a few minutes ago about leaving?

00:53:22.400 --> 00:53:24.320
Oh, just that. I'm getting married.

00:53:24.400 --> 00:53:26.080
- Married? - Who to?

00:53:26.080 --> 00:53:30.000
After all, Mr. Dietrich, that's rather my business, don't you think?

00:53:30.760 --> 00:53:37.110
- Who's going to be the best man? Danny Nearing? - I don't have to take that sort of thing from you and I don't intend to.

00:53:37.110 --> 00:53:41.820
Shut up, Bill. You're quite right. I'd like to go to bed now, Mrs. Dietrich, if you don't mind.

00:53:41.820 --> 00:53:47.170
Very well. As to your leaving, I'll naturally expect you to stay until I can make other arrangements.

00:53:47.170 --> 00:53:50.270
And if I were you, I think I'd tell the police where you're going.

00:53:50.270 --> 00:53:52.560
- Thank you. I will. - Good night.

00:53:52.560 --> 00:54:00.000
- Good night. - Maybe you'll give me a short synopsis of what this is all about.

00:54:09.310 --> 00:54:11.500
I found this in the hall. She said it was hers.

00:54:11.580 --> 00:54:14.540
Well, smoking cigarettes all over the house and breaking glasses.

00:54:14.620 --> 00:54:16.620
She's been having quite an evening for herself, hasn't she?

00:54:16.700 --> 00:54:19.510
But that's not the point. It's not her cigarette. It couldn't be.

00:54:19.590 --> 00:54:22.070
- What makes you think so? - Because she always wears a little lipstick.

00:54:22.150 --> 00:54:25.720
And there isn't any on that.

00:54:25.800 --> 00:54:29.240
I wonder if that's what Marucci meant when he asked me if I had a gun in the house.

00:54:30.700 --> 00:54:33.120
Maybe we'd better telephone the police and have them search the grounds.

00:54:33.280 --> 00:54:35.570
- Nervous? - I'm only thinking of you.

00:54:45.940 --> 00:54:47.240
Get me the sheriff's office.

00:55:00.090 --> 00:55:03.300
- The line is dead. - But he can't be. The operator answered you.

00:55:03.300 --> 00:55:07.590
- He's dead now. - You'd better drive into town and get the sheriff.

00:55:07.600 --> 00:55:09.500
- And leave you all alone? - My hero.

00:55:09.600 --> 00:55:13.100
If you have any sense, you'll just go upstairs and lock your bedroom door, as Marucci suggested.

00:55:13.200 --> 00:55:15.100
You'll stand guard outside, I suppose.

00:55:15.140 --> 00:55:19.400
No. I think I'll take a bath and curl up with a nice warm revolver.

00:55:19.490 --> 00:55:29.600
Ruth.

00:55:37.710 --> 00:55:41.070
Danny, they suspect something. You've got to get out of here now.

00:55:41.150 --> 00:55:42.670
It isn't safe for you to stay another minute.

00:55:43.350 --> 00:55:45.170
Staying here till I find what I came for.

00:55:45.490 --> 00:55:49.200
Oh, Danny. Danny, please, if you love me, get away from here before it's too late.

00:55:49.930 --> 00:55:52.070
Listen, use your head. Go back to town and wait.

00:55:52.250 --> 00:55:53.850
I'll check out of here tomorrow and meet you.

00:55:54.210 --> 00:55:57.960
We'll pick up a car and start west. It's what we always wanted to do.

00:55:58.140 --> 00:55:59.430
No, no. Well, I stay tonight.

00:56:00.700 --> 00:56:03.180
- You're a stubborn fool. - Where'll I stay?

00:56:04.890 --> 00:56:09.800
Alright. There's a greenhouse at the end of the garden. No one ever goes near it.

00:56:10.080 --> 00:56:14.170
On the grounds? But you said they suspect something is up. What if they phone the police?

00:56:14.290 --> 00:56:16.840
They won't. Not tonight.

00:56:20.410 --> 00:56:21.120
Danny.

00:56:52.490 --> 00:56:53.590
Have a lovely day.

00:57:10.590 --> 00:57:12.800
That girl's smarter than we gave her credit for being.

00:57:12.860 --> 00:57:15.940
There she goes, back in her regular daily routine with Grandma.

00:57:16.030 --> 00:57:18.040
Just as though nothing at all had happened last night.

00:57:18.140 --> 00:57:19.980
Yes, all the months she's been working here.

00:57:20.080 --> 00:57:21.680
I've never been able to get anything out of her.

00:57:21.780 --> 00:57:23.680
But yes, Mr. Diedrich, and no, Mr. Diedrich.

00:57:23.780 --> 00:57:25.730
Not that you haven't tried.

00:57:26.070 --> 00:57:28.200
If you cherish any fond hopes of leading me

00:57:28.300 --> 00:57:30.000
and the bulk of your brother's estate down that road,

00:57:30.000 --> 00:57:31.200
on that long red carpet.

00:57:31.300 --> 00:57:33.900
You'd better start disciplining that wandering eye of yours.

00:57:34.000 --> 00:57:36.780
Oh, behave, behave.

00:57:36.880 --> 00:57:38.780
- Has the man fixed the phone yet? - Yes, he's just left.

00:57:38.880 --> 00:57:41.080
Well, you're gonna telephone the police, you're gonna drive down.

00:57:41.180 --> 00:57:44.400
Well, I'm feeling rich and lazy. I think I'll phone.

00:58:00.760 --> 00:58:04.350
Here you are, honey, nice and cozy in the sun.

00:58:04.350 --> 00:58:10.650
- Dan, are you there? - But you'd never come.

00:58:10.650 --> 00:58:13.050
Stay back. They'll see you from the house.

00:58:13.050 --> 00:58:15.970
I brought you a sandwich. That's all I could get.

00:58:15.970 --> 00:58:18.940
They've been watching me like a pair of hawks.

00:58:18.940 --> 00:58:21.060
- Thanks. - Did you get any sleep?

00:58:21.060 --> 00:58:25.260
Oh, sure. Sometimes for as much as 15 minutes at a stretch.

00:58:25.260 --> 00:58:30.000
With my head on a sack of fertilizer and my feet in a lawnmower.

00:58:30.030 --> 00:58:34.290
- What are your plans? - I'll stay here 'til it gets dark.

00:58:34.390 --> 00:58:38.800
- It's the only thing I can do. - The police are liable to come.

00:58:38.800 --> 00:59:00.000
That'll be nice. Ruth, do you think you could go back to the house...

00:59:00.000 --> 00:59:02.240
and get me a pencil and paper without attracting attention.

00:59:02.520 --> 00:59:04.420
- What for? - Never mind what for.

00:59:04.720 --> 00:59:08.900
- I think I've discovered something. - What is it, Danny? Tell me.

00:59:09.380 --> 00:59:10.700
I'll tell you later.

00:59:11.490 --> 00:59:13.920
Can you get me that pencil and paper, or can't you?

00:59:14.430 --> 00:59:17.220
Yes, I think so, if it's that important to you.

00:59:17.430 --> 00:59:22.560
- If it wasn't, I wouldn't ask. - All right, Danny.

00:59:22.710 --> 00:59:25.400
Now, you be a good girl till I come back.

00:59:25.860 --> 00:59:29.470
- Whatever you do, stay out of sight. - Don't worry, I will.

00:59:35.600 --> 00:59:40.150
Mrs. Dietrich, will you talk to me with your eyes if I show you how?

00:59:42.500 --> 00:59:46.940
Listen carefully. I'm going through the alphabet.

00:59:47.070 --> 00:59:50.000
When I come to the letter you want, you blink once.

00:59:50.170 --> 00:59:53.600
We'll be able to spell out words. Understand?

00:59:54.330 --> 00:59:58.360
First, do you know anything about how your son died?

01:00:02.110 --> 01:00:03.090
You know who killed him.

01:00:06.440 --> 01:00:07.100
But you tell me.

01:00:12.670 --> 01:00:13.150
Why not?

01:00:16.030 --> 01:00:17.570
You mean you want to spell out your reasons?

01:00:24.090 --> 01:00:24.370
A.

01:00:25.900 --> 01:00:28.930
You mean the first letter of the word is A.

01:00:32.270 --> 01:00:34.010
Second, A.

01:01:17.630 --> 01:01:24.920
- D-A-F-R-A-I-D, afraid.

01:01:24.920 --> 01:01:27.070
- You're afraid?

01:01:27.070 --> 01:01:28.370
- Who you afraid of?

01:01:28.370 --> 01:01:29.320
- Danny, get back.

01:01:29.320 --> 01:01:30.000
- Wait a minute.

01:01:30.000 --> 01:01:31.380
Ruthie and the sheriff are here.

01:01:31.580 --> 01:01:32.900
Did you bring me that paper and pencil?

01:01:33.020 --> 01:01:35.400
No, there wasn't time. I thought it was more important to warn you.

01:01:35.480 --> 01:01:37.800
All right, you warned me. Now leave her here and go back and get them.

01:01:37.920 --> 01:01:40.860
You're out of your mind. I've got to take her back to the house.

01:01:41.160 --> 01:01:42.760
They might come looking for me to find you.

01:01:43.060 --> 01:01:44.440
I'll see what's going on.

01:01:44.680 --> 01:01:47.980
But for heaven's sake, whatever you do, keep undercover until you hear from me.

01:01:48.100 --> 01:01:50.660
Come back. A minute or two more won't matter.

01:01:51.010 --> 01:01:52.730
She was just going to tell me the name of the murderer.

01:01:53.740 --> 01:01:54.140
Ruth.

01:01:59.340 --> 01:02:00.000
Well, all those shit.

01:02:00.000 --> 01:02:02.680
The shenanigans last night add up to just one thing.

01:02:02.840 --> 01:02:05.220
Nearing's around here someplace and a girl knows where.

01:02:05.380 --> 01:02:07.440
Why would he be sucker enough to come back here?

01:02:07.560 --> 01:02:09.570
That's easy. They say she's given notice.

01:02:09.940 --> 01:02:12.380
He's got all that dough he swiped when he knifed your husband.

01:02:12.810 --> 01:02:17.090
They figure on beating it someplace and they just think New Jericho's a better jumping off place in the city.

01:02:17.540 --> 01:02:18.880
Not that they'll get very far.

01:02:19.040 --> 01:02:21.640
No, sirree. We'll get out a posse and surround the grounds.

01:02:21.880 --> 01:02:25.500
No, sirree. We won't get out no posse and we won't surround no grounds.

01:02:25.500 --> 01:02:29.800
We won't do any snooping around here and we won't bother our girlfriend with any more questions.

01:02:29.820 --> 01:02:29.960
Thank you.

01:02:30.190 --> 01:02:33.080
Would you mind telling us just where you intend to go from here?

01:02:33.580 --> 01:02:37.820
We're going back to New Jericho, and we're going to sit tight until tonight.

01:02:38.410 --> 01:02:40.410
Then, about 8:30 tonight...

01:02:40.440 --> 01:02:56.950
Mr. Marucci, all the sheriff's office telephones.

01:02:57.030 --> 01:02:58.180
Tell them we'll be at the country club.

01:02:58.260 --> 01:03:00.000
Yes, Mrs. Dietrich. And I hope we don't...

01:03:00.000 --> 01:03:02.940
find cigarettes and broken glasses lying around as we did last night.

01:03:03.100 --> 01:03:04.140
You won't, Mrs. Dietrich.

01:03:04.840 --> 01:03:26.240
Oh, so good.

01:03:26.770 --> 01:03:28.910
I think it wise, eh?

01:03:29.230 --> 01:03:29.980
What was that I get?

01:03:30.000 --> 01:03:35.670
- We're going to a dinner party at the country club. - By the way, Marucci, if you will allow me to make a suggestion.

01:03:35.670 --> 01:03:40.120
If you do happen to run across Danny Nearing, take my advice and shoot first.

01:03:40.120 --> 01:03:49.140
You'd like that, huh? Okay, folks, get moving. Tell 'em.

01:04:07.070 --> 01:04:10.130
I'd have had to stay there another five minutes ago to Stark, raving mad.

01:04:10.210 --> 01:04:10.570
I know.

01:04:10.610 --> 01:04:13.010
All day long, hour after hour, swallowing in that shed,

01:04:13.070 --> 01:04:15.970
not a drop of water, every nerve on my body on edge, and nothing happening.

01:04:16.130 --> 01:04:17.550
Well, darling, something's going to happen now.

01:04:17.970 --> 01:04:20.110
We're taking the other car and getting out of here.

01:04:20.410 --> 01:04:21.130
Everything's ready.

01:04:21.510 --> 01:04:23.130
The bags are packed, dark glasses.

01:04:23.350 --> 01:04:23.970
No rules.

01:04:26.100 --> 01:04:28.300
Danny, Danny, please don't say that.

01:04:28.970 --> 01:04:30.000
Believe me, I know what...

01:04:30.000 --> 01:04:31.550
That's what's best for us.

01:04:31.550 --> 01:04:35.420
We'll talk about it later.

01:04:35.420 --> 01:04:36.620
Come on, Danny, please.

01:04:36.620 --> 01:04:38.700
There's food in the kitchen, and while you're eating,

01:04:38.700 --> 01:04:41.140
I'll get out of my uniform and pick up my bag.

01:05:24.030 --> 01:05:26.050
There's nobody going to interrupt us this time.

01:05:34.830 --> 01:05:36.870
I want you to tell me who killed your son.

01:05:36.870 --> 01:05:40.010
There's nothing to be afraid of.

01:05:40.010 --> 01:05:42.310
I promise the moment you tell me,

01:05:42.310 --> 01:05:44.660
no matter who it is,

01:05:44.660 --> 01:05:48.980
I'll phone the police and have them move in fast.

01:05:48.980 --> 01:05:53.570
I'll give you the letters,

01:05:53.570 --> 01:05:57.080
and you signal to me the way we were doing this morning.

01:05:57.080 --> 01:05:58.230
A.

01:06:00.090 --> 01:06:06.470
B, C, D.

01:06:07.650 --> 01:06:14.850
Mrs. Dietrich, listen to me.

01:06:14.880 --> 01:06:17.480
Open your eyes, please.

01:06:19.200 --> 01:06:21.860
You're an old woman, you have much longer to live.

01:06:22.020 --> 01:06:24.640
Do you want me sent to the chair for something I didn't do?

01:06:24.980 --> 01:06:26.240
I couldn't have done.

01:06:30.120 --> 01:06:34.680
Was it Bill? Did he want his brother out of the way because of Alma?

01:06:37.010 --> 01:06:45.170
No, it wasn't Bill. Then it was Alma. To be free, to get his money.

01:06:45.480 --> 01:06:47.830
Was it because she wanted a divorce and he wouldn't give her one?

01:06:49.580 --> 01:06:58.390
No, that's wrong too. You're not telling the truth.

01:07:00.320 --> 01:07:01.400
It must have been one of them.

01:07:02.580 --> 01:07:03.600
Who else was in the house?

01:07:04.620 --> 01:07:05.580
Who else could it have been?

01:07:08.690 --> 01:07:21.050
You're satisfied.

01:07:22.370 --> 01:07:22.810
Ruth.

01:07:22.970 --> 01:07:24.370
You certainly asked for it.

01:07:25.100 --> 01:07:25.660
You didn't.

01:07:27.170 --> 01:07:27.490
You.

01:07:32.240 --> 01:07:35.030
He came in and found me taking the money out of the drawer.

01:07:35.900 --> 01:07:38.840
He hit me. It was a struggle.

01:07:39.160 --> 01:07:43.600
I reached for the first thing handy. It happened to be a knife.

01:07:44.050 --> 01:07:46.440
But how did she know?

01:08:04.960 --> 01:08:06.380
Yes, I knew she saw me.

01:08:07.250 --> 01:08:09.090
I came running in here afterwards.

01:08:09.250 --> 01:08:10.330
The door was open.

01:08:10.630 --> 01:08:12.830
I knew she'd seen me in the mirror.

01:08:13.950 --> 01:08:15.570
You realize she couldn't talk?

01:08:15.800 --> 01:08:16.780
You ran back to the bar.

01:08:17.700 --> 01:08:18.760
Yes, that's right.

01:08:20.130 --> 01:08:24.130
Is it going to make any difference?

01:08:26.350 --> 01:08:27.050
You and me.

01:08:28.520 --> 01:08:29.120
Couldn't?

01:08:30.510 --> 01:08:34.490
Then I don't care what happens. You love me, nothing else matters.

01:08:35.040 --> 01:08:37.140
I was trying to get that money for you, for us.

01:08:37.820 --> 01:08:40.040
You always said you would never marry me unless we had some money.

01:08:41.390 --> 01:08:45.400
I didn't mean to kill him, Danny. I'm not bad. I'm not a killer.

01:08:46.560 --> 01:08:51.260
Neither am I. When the police catch up with us, who are you going to let them arrest?

01:08:51.550 --> 01:08:51.910
Danny.

01:08:52.050 --> 01:08:52.210
Who?

01:08:52.930 --> 01:08:59.390
They're not going to catch up with us. We'll hide. We'll get out of the country. We'll fool them somehow.

01:08:59.390 --> 01:09:00.000
There isn't a chance.

01:09:00.000 --> 01:09:04.180
- We can make a run for it. - I'm not running. I don't have to now.

01:09:04.260 --> 01:09:14.790
- You're going to let them arrest me? - What else can I do?

01:09:14.870 --> 01:09:19.400
I've taken a lot from you, Danny, because I loved you and I thought you loved me.

01:09:19.480 --> 01:09:23.170
I don't love you. I've only known you two days.

01:09:23.250 --> 01:09:27.480
I'm not the man you think I am. I'm not Danny Nearing.

01:09:27.560 --> 01:09:30.000
My name is Frank Thompson and I'm married.

01:09:30.000 --> 01:09:32.600
to Virginia Morrison, that name over the doorbell.

01:09:32.680 --> 01:09:34.490
She's my wife.

01:09:34.550 --> 01:09:41.110
That's what you've been building up to all along, is it?

01:09:41.110 --> 01:09:43.020
This trick memory stuff,

01:09:43.100 --> 01:09:46.340
this not remembering things here at the house and all.

01:09:46.420 --> 01:09:48.440
I tried to tell you, there was an accident

01:09:48.520 --> 01:09:50.740
and somehow I became Danny Nearing.

01:09:50.740 --> 01:09:52.960
I built up a life as Danny Nearing.

01:09:53.010 --> 01:09:55.410
And then, with that blow on the head the other day,

01:09:55.410 --> 01:09:57.570
I became Frank Thompson again.

01:09:57.620 --> 01:10:00.000
What it... what it really amounts to.

01:10:00.000 --> 01:10:02.460
is that you've met this other woman

01:10:02.460 --> 01:10:04.480
and you're trying to brush me off

01:10:04.480 --> 01:10:05.840
with this phony alibi.

01:10:07.330 --> 01:10:10.660
Danny, after all, we've been to each other.

01:10:11.380 --> 01:10:12.560
After I stole for you,

01:10:13.200 --> 01:10:14.660
killed a man because I loved you.

01:10:15.170 --> 01:10:16.440
What kind of a love is it

01:10:16.440 --> 01:10:17.560
that would send me running away

01:10:17.560 --> 01:10:18.660
from a crime you committed?

01:10:19.440 --> 01:10:20.360
That would have stood by

01:10:20.360 --> 01:10:21.500
and let the police take me away

01:10:21.500 --> 01:10:22.320
to the electric chair?

01:10:32.170 --> 01:10:35.270
All right, Mr. Thompson, I guess it's my party from now on.

01:10:35.270 --> 01:10:37.030
I'm sorry, I'll help you all I can, you know.

01:10:37.030 --> 01:10:38.910
I'll handle it without any help from you, thanks.

01:10:38.910 --> 01:10:39.670
Ruth!

01:11:11.800 --> 01:11:16.840
- That isn't the answer, Ruth. - Do you know a better one, Mr. Thompson?

01:11:30.960 --> 01:11:54.060
i'm gonna die then hello big shot you're a little late oh i wouldn't say that grandma

01:11:54.060 --> 01:12:00.000
i'll ask grandma isn't there something we can do

01:12:04.760 --> 01:12:15.090
Danny, all that business about you being married, you were only kidding, weren't you?

01:12:16.590 --> 01:12:18.950
You don't love anybody but me, too.
